  { question: "Can a cannabis topical get you high?", answer: "Standard non-transdermal topicals (balms, salves, lotions, creams, bath products) typically do NOT produce a psychoactive effect because the cannabinoids don't reach the bloodstream in significant amounts. Transdermal patches are engineered to penetrate the skin barrier and enter the bloodstream — those CAN produce systemic effects including psychoactivity, depending on THC content." },
