  { question: "Are cannabis topicals safe for pets?", answer: "Cannabis topicals can be problematic around pets. Even non-psychoactive products contain cannabinoids that, if licked off a pet's paw or fur, can be absorbed through their digestive system and cause toxicity. The Pet Poison Helpline classifies THC-containing topicals as potentially toxic to dogs and cats. Store topicals like any cannabis product — in a closed container your pet cannot access." },
  { question: "Will a cannabis topical make me fail a drug test?", answer: "Standard non-transdermal topicals are highly unlikely to trigger a positive THC drug test, because the cannabinoids don't reach the bloodstream in significant amounts. Transdermal patches are engineered to deliver cannabinoids into the bloodstream and CAN trigger positive drug tests. If you are subject to drug testing for employment or other reasons, even small THC doses from patches can register. CBD-only topicals are the safest choice for drug-test-sensitive consumers." },
  { question: "How do I choose a topical at a Maine dispensary?", answer: "1) Identify your goal: localized muscle/joint soreness, skin inflammation, or sleep-related relaxation. 2) Decide THC:CBD ratio — CBD-only for daytime use, balanced for evening, THC-forward for stronger local effect. 3) Check the carrier — coconut oil and shea butter are common bases that determine skin feel. 4) Look at added ingredients — arnica, menthol, camphor, capsaicin, and essential oils augment the effect. 5) Verify the OCP license number on the label." },
  { question: "Do cannabis topicals expire?", answer: "Yes. Most topicals have a 12–24 month shelf life depending on the carrier and added preservatives. Check for a recommended-use or expiration date on the label (required per Title 28-B §701(1)(J)(3)). Store in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight. Discard if the product develops an off smell, color change, or mold." }
];
